  "description": "<p>Currently the only way to know if a given resource is a part of an AG is by looking for a</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\nLink: &lt;http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#ArchivalGroup&gt;;rel=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"type\"</span> </span></pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>header at each node in the containment hierarchy.  It would be convenient for clients to know whether a given resource is nested within an ArchivalGroup.</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>One approach would be to add a link header for AG nested resources that points to the archival group. So a GET to /my-archival-group/resourcA  for return the following header</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\nLink: &lt;http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/my-archival-group&gt;;rel=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"archival-group\"</span> </span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p> </p>",
